<title>PHILIPPINES: Investment inflows boost Philippine peso at close.</title>
<headline>Investment inflows boost Philippine peso at close.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Sept 10-------------------------</p>
<p>*Banks await next Central Bank move on rates</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso recovered some ground on Tuesday, drawing strength from dollar inflows for portfolio investments, traders said.</p>
<p>The peso closed at 26.228 to the dollar versus 26.235 on Monday. The day's average was 26.229 pesos from 26.232. Volume was lower at $105 million compared with $114.50 million.</p>
</text>
